    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0054" n="48" xml:id="pg48"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby, chargé, to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 37.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-04"><hi rendition="#italic">August 4, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received September 12.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    translation of a dispatch addressed to this legation on the 31st ultimo. A
                    similar dispatch was sent to the representatives of all the foreign powers.</p>
                <p>This dispatch is an explanation of the events which fed to the present war, and
                    is intended to justify China in the eyes of the world. In reply to the Yamên, I
                    have merely acknowledged receipt of the dispatch and stated that I would forward
                    to you a translation thereof.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. Denby</hi>, Jr.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d36-a1.xml" xpointer="d36-a1"/>
            </div>
